course: dictionary
lesson: 6612
title: Who were the Norse?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Norse is a word for people, a language and a set of stories from long ago. Read the clues around it. «Vikings were Norse people from Denmark, Norway and Sweden.» The Norse were people who lived in those countries, the Vikings among them.
explain: Now look at the word beside it. «Old Norse» is the language the Vikings spoke. «Norse myths» are the old stories about gods. Norse is an adjective when it describes something, and it is a noun when you talk about the people, so it always has a capital N.
explain: Clues can also come from a list. «Many English words come from Norse, like sky, egg, knife and Thursday.» Because these words come from Norse, the Norse language must have been spoken here long ago. Thursday means Thor's day, so Thor must be one of the Norse gods.
fact: The Norse were people from Norway, Denmark, Sweden and Iceland in the time of the Vikings.
fact: «Old Norse» is the language the Vikings spoke.
fact: «Norse myths» tell stories of gods like Odin, Thor and Loki.
fact: Many English words come from Old Norse, such as «sky», «egg» and «knife».
fact: Norse sailors, led by Leif Erikson, reached North America around the year 1000.
exercise: «Vikings were Norse people from Denmark, Norway and Sweden.» Where did the Norse people come from? | Brazil and Peru | Egypt and India | Spain and Italy | *Denmark, Norway and Sweden
exercise: «Many English words come from Norse, like sky, egg, knife and Thursday.» Which word is named after a Norse god? | Sky | Knife | *Thursday | Egg
exercise: Ella asks, «What is Old Norse?» Which answer is right? | A kind of boat | A type of food | A modern city | *The language the Vikings spoke
test: The Norse were farmers, traders and explorers who lived long ago. Which word describes these people? | Robin | Pippin | *Norse | Zeus
test: «Norse sailors led by Leif Erikson reached North America around the year 1000.» Where did the Norse sailors reach? | Antarctica | Australia | Africa | *North America
exam: Which sentence uses Norse correctly? | *Norse sailors reached North America around the year 1000 | I like norse pancakes with jam | Ella ate a norse sandwich for lunch | The norse sky is blue
